Did Technology Force a Homeless Woman to Verbalize Speech?
Was it voluntary or forced verbal speech?
Richard Pearson has experienced an extraordinary and complex campaign of torture. He continues to detail his experience
"Bitch, if we don't do it, then somebody else will."
In July 2026, Richard Pearson walked to the District of Columbia Department of Human Services Center on H Street to renew his paperwork for food assistance. With Union Station on his left, he walked down F St NE to 2nd St NE. 
He passed a Black homeless woman in her 30s at the intersection of F St NE and 2nd St NE. He shows her location in the image below. "I had seen her once before among the homeless population at the Martin Luther King Library." Pearson goes to the DHS Service.
"Consistent with all that I had been experiencing, the staff were very rude to me. After more than an hour of waiting, the lady at the counter refused to answer any of my questions after the first one, only directing me to turn in my paperwork to someone at a desk." In other words, Pearson didn't need to wait the hour. "The second woman at the desk was also rude. She didn't want to answer my questions either. She told me go to the window, which, of course, I had just come from." I left after giving her my paperwork. I wanted to know more about the renewal and resumption of food assistance.
Pearson took a different route on the way back. On the route to the DHS Service Center, he went north on 2nd St NE. On the way back, he went west on F St NE. The homeless woman was still there. Pearson is on the corner where the woman is. 
"Bitch, if we don't do it, somebody else will."
"She said it! Actually, verbalized it. I had been used to these inserted voices, but this woman actually said it."
The woman said nothing before and nothing afterwards. Pearson kept walking, though briefly looking at the woman. "She appeared catatonic when she said it, " explain Pearson. "It was very strange. That was all that she said."
Explanation
Initially, I thought it was gang activity. "I drew a connection between the rude people at the Service Center and this." There had been numerous baseless rumors about Pearson. Pearson thought that the woman was part of the gang. It could mean that the gang was behind at least some of his pinning and voice violence.
"I don't know. That's the nature of this invisible technology, but this woman can be found. She was on camera. This can be investigated. I know that she was homeless because I had seen her before." Pearson has the exact date because he turned in his government paperwork.
Pearson considers several details - 1) the woman was almost certainly homeless, 2) stationed exactly where he walked, and 3) appeared catatonic. He is increasingly drawn to another theory - forced verbalized speech. Pearson knows that pinning or behavioral manipulation is possible and that it's happening to homeless people.
The Homeless Man in Silver Spring, Maryland
Pearson describes a Black homeless man in downtown Silver Spring in March 2026. He was taking the Greyhound bus to Canada to escape asylum. "This Black homeless man was kicking his feet and gyrating his hands. This was quite out of the ordinary. I know homeless people. I noticed a Hispanic man who was approaching him from the side, then retreated to a bench. He then got on his phone. He was laughing hysterically as he sat across the man - looking at him and his phone." Pearson says that the man wasn't filming. He seemed to be interacting with the phone and the man. "It deeply disturbed me. I went up to the homeless man after the Hispanic man left and asked him if he was ok. These damn mind control weapons!" Pearson says that he attempted to take a picture of the Hispanic man, but he turned his head.
Ironically, Pearson was also a victim of mind control subsequently in Montreal, Canada. He recently wrote about it. 
Forced Verbal Speech and the Acknowledgment 
Pearson considers that forced speech is possible. "I don't know who did it or where it came from, but I am more confident than not that this exotic technology exists and was used on her."
But why?
"I believe that they were trying to justify what they were doing to me and why. They have told me more than once that they think I am a solider. It's torture. This is really outrageous." 
Something major is happening. Since July, Pearson has put together a terrifying picture. "This technology is out of control! For more than 40 years, the government has said anything. Congress has not inquired, not even a whiff of an investigatory interest. The federal courts have not recognized that the technology even exists. Victims have had their cases routinely tossed as "frivilous". So guess what now has happened? It has proliferated in different forms - the technology, the violence, the invisibility." Pearson's recent essay suggests something very serious is happening - a Neuro-arms war.
